# Security & config (full: docs/architecture/security.md)

- No secrets in git. `.env.example` holds placeholders or obviously local-only dev values; `.env` is gitignored.
- Every new env var: parsed + validated in `internal/config` (fail fast, `errors.Join` all problems), documented in `.env.example` and README.
- Secure defaults in code (`SSRF_PROTECTION=true`, `ALLOW_HTTP_CALLBACKS=false`); Compose may relax them explicitly for the local mock.
- API keys: store prefix + hash only, constant-time compare. Signing secrets: AES-256-GCM with `COURIER_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, returned once.
- Containers run as non-root, minimal base image, no build tools in the runtime stage.
- CI uses throwaway service credentials only; never echo secrets in workflow logs.
